1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,870
His own superiors did not want his plan.

2
00:00:02,910 --> 00:00:05,990
It led to victory over
France in six weeks.

3
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:12,550
Erich von Manstein was born in Berlin
in 1887 as Fritz Erich von Lewinski.

4
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:16,070
He grew up with his uncle and
from then on bore his name.

5
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:18,690
In the First World War
he was badly wounded.

6
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:23,220
In 1939 he proposed sending the
tanks through the Ardennes,

7
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:28,100
a forest region the French
thought tanks could barely cross.

8
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:32,810
The army command set the plan aside
and sent him off to command a corps.

9
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:35,260
But the plan still made
its way to the top.

10
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:40,520
In May 1940 the tanks pushed through the
Ardennes all the way to the Channel.

11
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:45,000
In 1941 Manstein took over
the 11th Army in Crimea.

12
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,020
On November 20 he signed an order.

13
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:53,410
In it he demanded that his soldiers
understand harsh measures against Jews.

14
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:58,320
In his area of command, Einsatzgruppe D
murdered tens of thousands of people.

15
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:04,420
In July 1942 Sevastopol fell, and
Manstein became a field marshal.

16
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:09,000
In December he was to relieve the
encircled 6th Army at Stalingrad.

17
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:12,570
His troops got to within
about 50 kilometers.

18
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:14,820
Then the attack was called off.

19
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:18,340
In March 1944 he was dismissed.

20
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:22,810
In 1949 he stood before a British
military court in Hamburg.

21
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:26,880
He was found guilty on
nine of seventeen counts,

22
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:29,580
partly because he had
not protected civilians.

23
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,070
The verdict: 18 years in prison.

24
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:34,860
By 1953 he was free again.

25
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:38,510
Two years later his book
appeared: Lost Victories.

26
00:01:38,550 --> 00:01:42,290
In it, the blame for the
defeats lay mostly with others.

27
00:01:42,330 --> 00:01:45,630
The crimes in his area of
command barely appeared.

28
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:49,060
For decades he was seen
as the clean strategist.

29
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,520
Historians see it differently today.

30
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:53,090
Did you know this story?

31
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:54,910
Tell us in the comments!
